{
  "agent": "holmes-mcp",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n1. Pod `notifications-worker-6784d8b8df-lk5l8` container `worker` crashed with exit code 1 (`Error`) and entered `CrashLoopBackOff` in `demo-apps`.\n2. Previous container logs state `ERROR notifications-worker: missing required setting SMTP_PASSWORD (environment variable is unset or empty)` and `FATAL notifications-worker: configuration invalid, exiting`.\n3. Deployment `CI-2459` rolled out `notifications-worker` v2.0.0 at 08:24:18Z, referencing `secretKeyRef` key `SMTP_PASSWORD` from Secret `notifications-smtp`.\n\n### Ruled-out leads\n1. OOMKills were ruled out because the container terminated with exit code 1 (`Error`) rather than exit code 137 (`OOMKilled`).\n2. Readiness probe failures were ruled out as the root cause because connection refused occurred only after the process exited on missing configuration.\n\n### Root cause\nDeployment `CI-2459` configured `notifications-worker` to require `SMTP_PASSWORD`, but optional `secretKeyRef` failed to populate the variable because Secret `notifications-smtp` lacks key `SMTP_PASSWORD`.\n\n### Recommended action\nThe notifications team should update Secret `notifications-smtp` or the Deployment's `secretKeyRef` to reference the correct secret key.",
